{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord","id":1488536,"title":"Is \"Wendigo\" censored on the Discord?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-30T23:11:28-07:00","id":1488536,"title":"Is \"Wendigo\" censored on the Discord?","content":"Someone posted this as evidence of such: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/slNOc\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.ph/slNOc</a><br /> <br /> Now calling a Werewolf tribe that when it has nothing remotly in common with the actual myths but still...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T01:55:44-07:00","id":1488542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord#post1488536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone posted this as evidence of such: <a href=\"https://archive.ph/slNOc\" target=\"_blank\">https://archive.ph/slNOc</a><br /> <br /> Now calling a Werewolf tribe that when it has nothing remotly in common with the actual myths but still...</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Note: European and White. Just offering my thoughts.</b><br /> <br /> Different cultures have different rules when it comes to words related to their religion. The Younger Brother has a lot of ties to the creature, as the Younger Brother is a Native American/First Nations tribe and at least the Revised tribebook does discuss the creature.<br /> <br /> I doubt the actual word is censored, just forbidden in that particular discord server. Still, I consider it a justified choice as the word has power and there are other words we no longer use anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T01:56:31-07:00","id":1488543,"title":"","content":"Members of the real indigenous people for whom that myth is part of their cultural background have repeatedly called for it to stop being used; both as fodder for outsider fantasy/fiction, and indiscriminately as a term. The association of it with werewolves in particular (not unique to WtA btw) is something seen as extremely offensive to the people the myth has been appropriated from.<br /> <br /> There's no way for Discord to simply ban the world outright (you own screen cap shows it no less!) but most WtA social spaces are pushing to cease using it, and it's expected to get retconned out of W5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T03:42:24-07:00","id":1488548,"title":"","content":"Is the only the name the problem, or the whole following the Cannibal spirit spiel? Because in theory if it's just the name we could jut go with Ithaqqua?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T06:59:15-07:00","id":1488562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488543#post1488543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Members of the real indigenous people for whom that myth is part of their cultural background have repeatedly called for it to stop being used; both as fodder for outsider fantasy/fiction, and indiscriminately as a term. The association of it with werewolves in particular (not unique to WtA btw) is something seen as extremely offensive to the people the myth has been appropriated from.<br /> <br /> There's no way for Discord to simply ban the world outright (you own screen cap shows it no less!) but most WtA social spaces are pushing to cease using it, and it's expected to get retconned out of W5.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right, that makes sense. It's just encouragement. These anti-woke pearl-clutchers are getting out of hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T07:50:58-07:00","id":1488565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488562#post1488562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right, that makes sense. It's just encouragement. These anti-woke pearl-clutchers are getting out of hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think wanting to respect the culture of another or your own culture is pearl-clutching. There are a lot of indigenous people helping with the Cyber Record, so I'm trusting them to know whether the word is allowed or not.<br /> <br /> Or even anti-woke.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T17:06:33-07:00","id":1488620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488565#post1488565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think wanting to respect the culture of another or your own culture is pearl-clutching. There are a lot of indigenous people helping with the Cyber Record, so I'm trusting them to know whether the word is allowed or not.<br /> <br /> Or even anti-woke.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, the anti-woke are the ones complaining that this is censorship of some sort. Sorry for the confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T20:21:31-07:00","id":1488648,"title":"","content":"Just, like, my opinion, but if WtA is going to stop using words or names due to offensive implications, I'd start with <i>Metis</i>.<br /> <br /> This is a term used up here in Canada for people descended from both Indigenous and &quot;Settlers.&quot; Even today, I find the way it was used in Werewolf as unbelievable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 08-01-2022, 03:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-31T22:56:06-07:00","id":1488668,"title":"","content":"That is also suspected to be on the chopping block as well.<br /> <br /> The names of Younger and Older Brother get a bit more attention because there's a conflicting issue of them being names that, in-universe, are ones the characters as supposed to want to self-identify with as a sign of their deep connections to their human kinfolk. And the issue with the Garou-born are also pretty well tread compared to First Nation/Indigenous peoples/etc. starting to be more vocal in gaming spaces around the cultural misappropriation of their beliefs by mainstream European cultures. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, we don't have to rank terms in order of which we would ax if we only got to ax one of them. The message seemed to get through to Paradox that all three should be addressed in W5.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T03:40:32-07:00","id":1488679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488620#post1488620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, the anti-woke are the ones complaining that this is censorship of some sort. Sorry for the confusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry. Did not mean to accuse you.<br /> <br /> And yeah, metis def. should be changed as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T06:00:33-07:00","id":1488688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488668#post1488668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is also suspected to be on the chopping block as well.<br /> <br /> The names of Younger and Older Brother get a bit more attention because there's a conflicting issue of them being names that, in-universe, are ones the characters as supposed to want to self-identify with as a sign of their deep connections to their human kinfolk. And the issue with the Garou-born are also pretty well tread compared to First Nation/Indigenous peoples/etc. starting to be more vocal in gaming spaces around the cultural misappropriation of their beliefs by mainstream European cultures.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, we don't have to rank terms in order of which we would ax if we only got to ax one of them. The message seemed to get through to Paradox that all three should be addressed in W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Metis are out based on the Achilli interview that is our biggest source of info on the weirdness that W5 will be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Two native american cultural advisors on the team<br /> Tribes as less tied to geography and culture and more to concept<br /> Focus on younger werewolves trying to reclaim what was lost<br /> World is fucked up horribly but not post apocalyptic<br /> Umbra as a hostile place, caerns cut off from the spirit world<br /> haglust (spelling?) -&gt; opposite to Harano, hysterical zeal, embodied by a new antagonist tribe that may or may not be right<br /> Focus on renown as something that empowers the Garou<br /> Getting rid of Metis and Pure Breed<br /> No more Garou Shall not Mate with Garou </div> </div> </div>Heavy, you always know everything, got a good source on why the &quot;Ice &amp; Cannibalism&quot; Spirit is problematic and which part of it is an issue for the people for who it's a taboo? I don't see using that tribe any time soon due to their rather strict geographic linkage, but it'd be useful as a starting point to see where to go with them when I do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":".  Just a reminder of the stuff rome the interview 08-01-2022, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T06:00:40-07:00","id":1488689,"title":"","content":"We already have confirmation Metis are removed as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T08:49:36-07:00","id":1488702,"title":"","content":"Personally, even if metis aren't in W5, people are still going to use them in W20 and such games. So finding an alternative term would still be good.<br /> <br /> As much as crinos-born sounds good, I feel it is too positive to be a general term for the breed. Crinos is technically the holiest form a garou can take, so using it in the breed name for the deformed litany-breaches does not really fit. Maybe something like Malus (Apple/evil) or such?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T14:04:16-07:00","id":1488734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488688#post1488688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis are out based on the Achilli interview that is our biggest source of info on the weirdness that W5 will be.</div> </div> </div> </div>When it's in an actual gaming product, I'll state it more absolutely. Justin has said more recently that Breed is no longer going to be a mechanical distinction in W5, and basically is only there as a descriptive distinction due to legacy issues. Even if they stop using the word Metis, it doesn't mean everything wrong about how things are now is going to be addressed fully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...got a good source on why the &quot;Ice &amp; Cannibalism&quot; Spirit is problematic and which part of it is an issue for the people for who it's a taboo? </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> It's taboo. That is the issue in broader context. <br /> <br /> Seriously you can Google, &quot;Is Wendigo racist?&quot; and at least half of the first page should be decent sources on how badly mainstream culture has mangled the mythology and abandoned lessons meant to be taught by it to add to the pop culture list of monsters for white heroes to slay/defeat/whatever. Anything where the wendigo isn't pure evil is a problem.<br /> <br /> If you asked a knowledgeable source about what Algonquin people would call the Eater-of-Souls head of the Triatic Wyrm in WtA that didn't know about the names of other things in the game, they'd probably say wendigo is a good term for that. It is a spiritual embodiment of greed and selfishness that unendingly seeks to consume everything to fill its spiritual void, and knows only evil to do so. The process of becoming a fomor is extremely on point for how getting possessed/cursed by the wendigo is told by native cultures.<br /> <br /> It is as on-the-nose as if there was a Tribe in WtA named, &quot;Antichrist worshiping baby murderers&quot; that's supposed to have deep and meaningful connections to Christians; follow Christian traditions and teachings, and represent Christians in the game. That's the level of getting it wrong we're dealing with here.<br /> <br /> The other two North American Tribes' names are slightly less bad, but still bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488702#post1488702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, even if metis aren't in W5, people are still going to use them in W20 and such games. So finding an alternative term would still be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou-born as worked well enough. It plays directly into the phrasing of the Litany and thus doesn't have the conflicting messaging presented with using Crinos-born.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T14:43:35-07:00","id":1488736,"title":"","content":"I'm all for getting rid of eugenics as a game mechanic. Same for the offensive names.<br /> However, removing what are effectively disabled people from the game now would stink of sweeping things under the rug, especially after they were in the game for so long. I would rather have them keep the concept, and instead emphasize it as a point of conflict within changer cultures for players to discuss and explore. If they want to address and deal with the cultural appropriation issues, it's not too much to ask to do the same for disabled people, imo.<br /> <br /> Edit: oops, maybe I misunderstood and they just plan on changing the name? If so, my bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 08-01-2022, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T14:55:47-07:00","id":1488737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488734#post1488734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you asked a knowledgeable source about what Algonquin people would call the Eater-of-Souls head of the Triatic Wyrm in WtA that didn't know about the names of other things in the game, they'd probably say wendigo is a good term for that. It is a spiritual embodiment of greed and selfishness that unendingly seeks to consume everything to fill its spiritual void, and knows only evil to do so. The process of becoming a fomor is extremely on point for how getting possessed/cursed by the wendigo is told by native cultures.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that's what I was interested in and pretty much explains it to me. There's nothing on general mythology or wikipedia on it,and honestly &quot;Is Wendigo Racist&quot; is not a search string I would have gone for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T16:54:23-07:00","id":1488746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488736#post1488736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, removing what are effectively disabled people from the game now would stink of sweeping things under the rug, especially after they were in the game for so long.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been debated in previous threads, I think the problem is the idea that &quot;splat = representation.&quot; You can play homids and lupus with disabilities that have them for the same reasons people have them in general instead of it being a cursed state and all the problems that causes.<br /> <br /> It's more the simple enough to make an inter-Tribal Camp that has championed disability issues in Garou society for a long time, as even Garou born without any can easily get them but not lose their value to the Nation without having to have a more modern sensibility around disability issues. There is a tenet of the Litany that already causes a place to explore disability topics without forcing really nasty discriminatory tropes into the game: How many Battle Scars before you're suffering your people to tend your sickness? How many bouts of Harano? What room is there for people born with disabilities in Garou society?<br /> <br /> We have ample material in the game without the Metis Breed to explore these issues. We've been able to explore them regardless of Breed since the first Flaw lists were printed.<br /> <br /> Sometimes any representation is better than no representation. But we're in a situation where we can get good representation even if it means sacrificing the old representation that was seriously flawed but loved for at least trying at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: oops, maybe I misunderstood and they just plan on changing the name? If so, my bad. </div> </div> </div>We don't have a concrete thing yet. Paradox's statements lean more towards no more Metis at all, but many could also be read as just changing the name as an option.<br /> <br /> Remember that W5 is currently in it's second attempt. The first version was dumped, and Paradox changed developers, so we have some mixed signals between when W5 was first announced, and how thing are probably going now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488737#post1488737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks, that's what I was interested in and pretty much explains it to me. There's nothing on general mythology or wikipedia on it,and honestly &quot;Is Wendigo Racist&quot; is not a search string I would have gone for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've found that sometimes such... crude... search terms get past generic sources that can obscure minority voices on the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T23:32:30-07:00","id":1488765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488746#post1488746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes any representation is better than no representation. But we're in a situation where we can get good representation even if it means sacrificing the old representation that was seriously flawed but loved for at least trying at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also give any vampire a derangement and remove the Malkavians in an attempt to get rid of fish-malks. I don't want to repeat the discussions that were had in other threads, I just think confronting the issue worked better in case of the Malks, and I think it would work better here. Ultimately it's up to the authors.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T00:18:24-07:00","id":1488766,"title":"","content":"The problem with that comparison, is that fish-malks are a player phenomenon. The books don't actively encourage this and implore the players to take their weakness seriously. Fish-malks only come up in the sense of Malks pulling a prank on other vampires who don't understand mental illness so they remain underestimated.<br /> <br /> The issue with the Metis as regards to disabled representation is that the bad aspects of that representation are directly from the text. Players subvert the text by playing Metis/playing characters that treat Metis less extremely than the books call for, rather than taking things to an absurd degree.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T08:04:11-07:00","id":1488821,"title":"","content":"Well, a recent <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1554457301301567491\" target=\"_blank\">tweet</a> seems to confirm there's only Lupus and Homid breeds. I disagree with the decision, but we will see how it plays out.<br /> <br /> Will be interesting to see how they treat Changing Breeds that have a different attitude towards children between changers, too.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T10:49:24-07:00","id":1488853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1488821#post1488821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a recent <a href=\"https://twitter.com/jachilli/status/1554457301301567491\" target=\"_blank\">tweet</a> seems to confirm there's only Lupus and Homid breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>OKAY, this is VERY interesting to me.<br /> <br /> Because one of the common gripes about WtA I've seen over the years is that the lupus breed implies bestiality. The TV Tropes page for WtA has a section showing concern over the breed being shock jockeying. So I was not expecting them to keep lupus due to the implications it has, since W5 IS trying to smooth things out.<br /> <br /> Mind, I'm happy they kept lupus.<br /> <br /> In addition, from the tweet I get the feeling lupus no longer have their CC limits. Which is another set of interesting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T20:02:47-07:00","id":1490213,"title":"","content":"So what are everyones' thoughts on people wanting to play Werewolf knowing it contains problematic terms? I have some friends that like the WtA system, and like the general story of the world (most books we have are for revised edition) and we're looking to play again as a small break from D&amp;D. However we do like to live stream our game sessions, not that we get many viewers, and putting on a show for others isn't our main objective, we play for our own enjoyment and streaming is just something we're playing around with on the side.<br /> <br /> How would you people approach this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4674-ammayhem","name":"AMmayhem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4674_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-14T20:56:09-07:00","id":1490214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AMmayhem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490213#post1490213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are everyones' thoughts on people wanting to play Werewolf knowing it contains problematic terms? I have some friends that like the WtA system, and like the general story of the world (most books we have are for revised edition) and we're looking to play again as a small break from D&amp;D. However we do like to live stream our game sessions, not that we get many viewers, and putting on a show for others isn't our main objective, we play for our own enjoyment and streaming is just something we're playing around with on the side.<br /> <br /> How would you people approach this?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have alternative words to use. Crinos-born, Younger Brother, Older Brother,etc. As for the general issues? I honestly think as long as the players and you do their research, it should be fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T02:38:37-07:00","id":1490235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AMmayhem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490213#post1490213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are everyones' thoughts on people wanting to play Werewolf knowing it contains problematic terms? I have some friends that like the WtA system, and like the general story of the world (most books we have are for revised edition) and we're looking to play again as a small break from D&amp;D. However we do like to live stream our game sessions, not that we get many viewers, and putting on a show for others isn't our main objective, we play for our own enjoyment and streaming is just something we're playing around with on the side.<br /> <br /> How would you people approach this?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a big planet to play on. It's easy to place your games somewhere you know about and use different terms for names considered offensive. Do a bit of research about the places you run games in, lean into what you know/learn and embrace the cultures and mythologies the game is inspired by. It's going to make your make much better and it's not going to hurt anyone in the process <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T03:47:25-07:00","id":1490241,"title":"","content":"RPGs are, in many ways, easier to solve than most media that hasn't aged well. RPGs are designed with customization and interactivity in-mind. I can decide what to call a group at my table far more easily than I can alter the coding of a video game, or redub a film, to try to not have these words diminish the fun of the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> But this falls into the same issue with all older media: acknowledge the problems as they are, self-reflect on your own personal boundaries, discuss the boundaries of those that will be taking part of the media in question with you if any, do not defend the problems as not being problems when talking about the media in public. Some people's personal boundaries mean they cannot enjoy WtA, and that's valid, other people can find ways to deal with the problematic stuff but still play, and that's also valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T08:07:05-07:00","id":1490257,"title":"","content":"I am not happy with the idea of just cutting the Garou-born out, and I'm not happy with completely cutting out everything that qualifies one's birth instead of just the mechanics that would justify the prejudice.<br /> <br /> Garou society also has its problems, and it was one of the best lines to explore the problems related to those themes. Things like Pure-Breed giving actual benefits was certainly a bad choice, but just eliminating the whole concept <b>does</b> reeks of sweeping problems under the rug.<br /> <br /> Now, if they make something to deal with such representations, great. It may come out better and <b>maybe</b> not come across as erasure. If they simply retcon the issues and the new stuff doesn't come out really good, the stench of erasure won't be so easy to ignore. If they do not even try to create new representation besides just making those character concepts &quot;possible&quot;, but without any exploration, then I'll be seriously pissed.<br /> <br /> The old representation did got a lot of things right. Namely, the actual kind of prejudice we face. People <b>are</b> deemed as failures for being disabled, parents, specially mothers, <b>are</b> frequently judged for the disabilities of their children, disabled children, specially babies, are killed to this day even in the richest countries, sometimes right after the birth and reported as stillborn, and those that live are treated as liabilities and weight for most of society for the rest of our lives, with varying degrees of subtlety (or none at all). Heck, disabled people that commit suicide are frequently depicted by media as tragic heroes that did the right thing by taking their own lives instead of their desperation getting any serious examination.<br /> <br /> Werewolf did a very good job in showcasing how some common beliefs of our society are wrong just by having the Garou being blatant about them, and the Garou-born were a big part of this. I still don't feel confident about what we'll see in the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:14:47-07:00","id":1490388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AMmayhem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490213#post1490213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are everyones' thoughts on people wanting to play Werewolf knowing it contains problematic terms? I have some friends that like the WtA system, and like the general story of the world (most books we have are for revised edition) and we're looking to play again as a small break from D&amp;D. However we do like to live stream our game sessions, not that we get many viewers, and putting on a show for others isn't our main objective, we play for our own enjoyment and streaming is just something we're playing around with on the side.<br /> <br /> How would you people approach this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf society is supposed to be wrong and backwards about a lot of things, so I'm opposed to the dumping of &quot;metis&quot;. Perhaps individual player-character werewolves could oppose the term, but player-characters are supposed to be the exception to the norm. Werewolf society as a whole should keep right on being backwards.<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;wendigo&quot; isn't a term that makes any sense. It's not backwards or reactionary, it's just wrong in a way that doesn't make any sense. There's no werewolf society-wide bigotry against the &quot;Wendigo&quot;, and they certainly wouldn't use the term for themselves.<br /> <br /> So I think you have to go on a case by case basis and basically ask, &quot;is this term rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, or is it just dumb and nonsensical?&quot; Metis is rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, and wendigo is just dumb.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:25:01-07:00","id":1490390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490388#post1490388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf society is supposed to be wrong and backwards about a lot of things, so I'm opposed to the dumping of &quot;metis&quot;. Perhaps individual player-character werewolves could oppose the term, but player-characters are supposed to be the exception to the norm. Werewolf society as a whole should keep right on being backwards.<br /> <br /> That said, &quot;wendigo&quot; isn't a term that makes any sense. It's not backwards or reactionary, it's just wrong in a way that doesn't make any sense. There's no werewolf society-wide bigotry against the &quot;Wendigo&quot;, and they certainly wouldn't use the term for themselves.<br /> <br /> So I think you have to go on a case by case basis and basically ask, &quot;is this term rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, or is it just dumb and nonsensical?&quot; Metis is rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, and wendigo is just dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not about IC issues, this is about the issues that using those words OOCly creates and who it alienates.<br /> <br /> Essentially, if there are to be tribes based on Native American nations, then it should be made sure the people from those cultures can actually play the game without feeling their culture is spit on. The use of the W-word is that, as is the use of the term metis.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:41:04-07:00","id":1490394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490388#post1490388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis is rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, and wendigo is just dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Metis&quot; means &quot;of mixed parentage&quot;, which is also pretty dumb when you consider it's the opposite of what it tries to describe. On top of dumping incestous connotations on a real group of people. The Garou are a lot older than the french language and there could easily be a different traditional term, so I have no issue with dropping Metis as a descriptor.<br /> <br /> As I said before, I disagree with dropping the concept as a whole for the same reasons others mentioned, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> in particular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:40:56-07:00","id":1490438,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is the whole WtA lexicon doesn't make any sort of sense. Words are picked from many time periods and many areas of the world with minimal eye towards consistency, original usage, modern usage, or how well it reflects why the Garou would use a term.<br /> <br /> While it isn't going to solve everything wrong with the game, there's a lot of low intensity work that can be done reevaluating the whole game's lexicon using a simple basis: The Garou all speak the Garou tongue, and that is the default &quot;word&quot; for any given concept. But since humans can't comprehend said language, the lexicon is a common translation for the given time and area assume in the text.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T15:13:51-07:00","id":1490445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490438#post1490438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of the problem is the whole WtA lexicon doesn't make any sort of sense. Words are picked from many time periods and many areas of the world with minimal eye towards consistency, original usage, modern usage, or how well it reflects why the Garou would use a term.<br /> <br /> While it isn't going to solve everything wrong with the game, there's a lot of low intensity work that can be done reevaluating the whole game's lexicon using a simple basis: The Garou all speak the Garou tongue, and that is the default &quot;word&quot; for any given concept. But since humans can't comprehend said language, the lexicon is a common translation for the given time and area assume in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would make sense, but I think it's a level of forethought that I don't expect from the current crowd. If they introduced a nice say page or even two page spread with different names for say Fomori (and all the other common terms) in different parts of the world and in the Garou tongue, I'd be quite happy with that way of internalising the loan from everything approach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T15:35:39-07:00","id":1490446,"title":"","content":"The worse part is that a good amount of the work was already done in things like the Tribebooks where they introduced custom lexicons (though context is still good, I'm still boggled by people that tried to claim that &quot;Modi&quot; and &quot;Ahroun&quot; were different in Garou Tongue). We already have lots of examples in the books of different local/cultural terms for things without needing to do a bunch of research on new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T16:44:11-07:00","id":1490455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490388#post1490388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think you have to go on a case by case basis and basically ask, &quot;is this term rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, or is it just dumb and nonsensical?&quot; Metis is rooted in werewolf society being backwards and reactionary, and wendigo is just dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490438#post1490438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it isn't going to solve everything wrong with the game, there's a lot of low intensity work that can be done reevaluating the whole game's lexicon using a simple basis: The Garou all speak the Garou tongue, and that is the default &quot;word&quot; for any given concept. But since humans can't comprehend said language, the lexicon is a common translation for the given time and area assume in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that sense I think <i>Forsaken</i> did a good job by assuming Faux-Friggin-<u>Sumerian</u> for their lexicon. If for no other reason because it will avoid inconsistencies in how the idea is applied on translation (named, instead of making local terms many translators just keep the English ones, either translated but making no sense because the context is difference, or not even that and completely missing the point).<br /> <br /> \u200bThe best option would be doing as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> suggested, but short of that faux-whatever-dead-language just requires a dictionary or an automatic translator and have a result that still feels like being an actual language. But otherwise yeah, we have a huge problem with Werewolf lexicon being the worse nonsensical word salad in the whole WoD, and that is a really low bar.<br /> <br /> On the matter of &quot;Metis&quot;, though, and many other terms related to their society being backwards, the book could have two lexicons, one used by the more socially aware Garou and the other by yer old farts who cling to both traditional prejudice and, unfortunately, power. That would both help ease things and contextualize old terms without retconning the game to sweep problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T13:16:49-07:00","id":1490534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490455#post1490455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically that.<br /> <br /> <br /> In that sense I think <i>Forsaken</i> did a good job by assuming Faux-Friggin-<u>Sumerian</u> for their lexicon. If for no other reason because it will avoid inconsistencies in how the idea is applied on translation (named, instead of making local terms many translators just keep the English ones, either translated but making no sense because the context is difference, or not even that and completely missing the point).<br /> <br /> \u200bThe best option would be doing as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a> suggested, but short of that faux-whatever-dead-language just requires a dictionary or an automatic translator and have a result that still feels like being an actual language. But otherwise yeah, we have a huge problem with Werewolf lexicon being the worse nonsensical word salad in the whole WoD, and that is a really low bar.<br /> <br /> On the matter of &quot;Metis&quot;, though, and many other terms related to their society being backwards, the book could have two lexicons, one used by the more socially aware Garou and the other by yer old farts who cling to both traditional prejudice and, unfortunately, power. That would both help ease things and contextualize old terms without retconning the game to sweep problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't exactly faux-Sumerian. It usually took even older Akkadian words and back-shifted them through Grimm's law to make them sound more guttural, though if the word had a lot of sibilants, it would often end up unaltered.<br /> <br /> (Used to try very hard to make stuff in W:tF, but it was rather exhausting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-17T13:30:11-07:00","id":1490537,"title":"","content":"While Forsaken does allow the fun of diving into conlang for people that are into that, it important doesn't require you to actually learn it to play the game.<br /> <br /> Apocalypse doesn't need it (and copying Forsaken would just add to other headaches). We know that Garou Tongue includes things like body posture using parts humans don't have, scent, and other such details that us humans playing the game can't actually replicate anyway. Since the Garou have a universal language, but one that's difficult to use outside of one form, and that's a form they shouldn't be spending all their time in (both the Veil and the modifier to Frenzy difficulties), all the change the setting needs is the idea that in-character Garou Tongue is generally subject to local variations in how it gets translated, while the mechanical text uses somewhat archaic terms to help them stand out in the text.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T07:16:09-07:00","id":1490604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490537#post1490537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">all the change the setting needs is the idea that in-character Garou Tongue is generally subject to local variations in how it gets translated, while the mechanical text uses somewhat archaic terms to help them stand out in the text.</div> </div> </div> </div>The specific problem with that idea is that it needs at least two or three standing examples to work as intended, potentially bloating the lexicon.<br /> <br /> If you states that such variations exist, but doesn't show it, it does becomes hard to visualize and many readers won't really grasp the idea. This gets worse with translations, though, because they're more likely to try to translate the sample terms instead of coming with their own. They'll either make translations that aren't context-appropriate, or worse, not even translate some of those terms to keep the &quot;mood&quot;.<br /> <br /> A very simple and direct example of this translation issue, to this day many Brazilian fans complain about the term for Pack in Forsaken, that here is distinct from the term for Pack used in Apocalypse. Forsaken uses &quot;Alcateia&quot;, while Apocalypse uses &quot;Matilha&quot;. The thing is, the term from Apocalypse is actually technically correct, but a terrible translation, because <b>it is meant for dogs, not wolves</b>.<br /> <br /> So, that's the kind of problem with a simpler lexicon, but there are others. It isn't so bad with things like Vampire, where the core theme is easier to grasp (archaic and French-y), but Werewolf has no core theme in the lexicon. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1182_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1182\" data-vbnamecard=\"1182\">Asmodai</a>'s idea would help by making three examples of each word as they lessen the weight of individual terms and make people more comfortable with variations. <b>short of that</b> I think a conlang would be a better idea than a word salad, even if one that more directly recognizes itself to be just a word salad.<br /> <br /> Even the current lexicon could be just kept if they make the triple lexicon, as it may be the common lexicon in the NY area or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T10:45:00-07:00","id":1490631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490604#post1490604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The specific problem with that idea is that it needs at least two or three standing examples to work as intended, potentially bloating the lexicon.</div> </div> </div> </div>The lexicon is already artificially bloated with a large number of terms that are archaic (and some are rare spellings of those on top of it) and have simple modern equivalents that don't really need definitions in a lexicon.<br /> <br /> This is also easily addressed by something the books already do: having different sections in the lexicon. Many concepts get repeated in a lexicon with a &quot;common,&quot; &quot;formal/archaic,&quot; and &quot;vulgar/slang,&quot; subsections without making individual entries bloated.<br /> <br /> For WtA, you can also reduce the feeling of bloat by having a short sidebar in each Tribal 2-page with a set of terms that are commonly used in the Tribe thanks to a common trade language in their past that most Garou in that area speak because of their wide ranging duties. About a dozen terms in each Tribe's write up is more than enough examples to show off the idea that system/out-of-game/etc. terms are meant to be translated locally. Thus it becomes shown.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This gets worse with translations, though, because they're more likely to try to translate the sample terms instead of coming with their own. </div> </div> </div>It seems easier if the text says, &quot;this is just the language of the books, and locals will generally use local translations,&quot; rather than making it seem like every Garou on Earth knows what the word &quot;Ronin&quot; means regardless of their exposure to Japanese culture (or some inane idea that the Garou inspired the Japanese word somehow, even though the WtA use of the word is not the original Japanese meaning of the word, but a later common use that was popularized in media).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A very simple and direct example of this translation issue, to this day many Brazilian fans complain about the term for Pack in Forsaken, that here is distinct from the term for Pack used in Apocalypse. Forsaken uses &quot;Alcateia&quot;, while Apocalypse uses &quot;Matilha&quot;. The thing is, the term from Apocalypse is actually technically correct, but a terrible translation, because <b>it is meant for dogs, not wolves</b>. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what this illustrates. Especially if it's meant to be a point against what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>short of that</b> I think a conlang would be a better idea than a word salad, even if one that more directly recognizes itself to be just a word salad. </div> </div> </div>And my point is that the books already contain 5-6 versions of localized words for various concepts as it is. If one were to do a complete lexicon of WtA, you'd already have at least three examples for most in-character terms, if not many more, to choose from. This work is already done. A conlang is new work, a lot of work, and somehow needs to differentiate itself from Forsaken's conlang.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T20:57:06-07:00","id":1490677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488536-is-wendigo-censored-on-the-discord?p=1490631#post1490631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems easier if the text says, &quot;this is just the language of the books, and locals will generally use local translations,&quot; rather than making it seem like every Garou on Earth knows what the word &quot;Ronin&quot; means regardless of their exposure to Japanese culture (or some inane idea that the Garou inspired the Japanese word somehow, even though the WtA use of the word is not the original Japanese meaning of the word, but a later common use that was popularized in media).</div> </div> </div> </div>In theory. In practice it too regularly doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> Now, since you're saying that the bloat is not a problem, I'm just explaining my point on translations.<br /> <br /> As much as you say in the very text that things shouldn't be taken at face value in some sense, in this case that you shouldn't try to just translate the same term, but instead the idea behind the text, in practice it is the kind of work most translators won't do, specially when they're translating a game and they have to convince a game publisher to roll with their work. Lexicons end up being some of the places where it is more likely for bad translations to happen.<br /> <br /> With a limited lexicon that gives the impression of a given term being really formal/official/what everyone does, this not only goes even worse, it also taints player perception. Foreign players are just as likely to take things at face value instead of reading between the lines, even when the book directly says you should, but they have the added problem that they mostly won't ever know how the original text was, they only know the translation, adding a new layer to the problem.<br /> <br /> My illustration with the translation of Pack is that, because the book only uses one term and it has this sense of formality, almost no player ever questioned its translation as &quot;Matilha&quot;. It is not that they didn't know it was specifically a dog pack, it is that they assumed it was a dog pack for a reason and this reason made any other option objectively wrong. Granted, pack is hard to have more than one term in English, but even then they could have said that in some states they call them just &quot;bands&quot;, while in Louisiana &quot;Meute&quot; is common.<br /> <br /> The point is similar to a &quot;show, don't tell&quot;. If you just tell people that terms change, they'll still cling to the given terms adamantly. And when you add the layer of translation, this problem reaches a point you're not used to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T23:08:38-07:00","id":1490679,"title":"","content":"The &quot;bad translation of the text&quot; argument isn't working for me, because you're essentially saying that it happens anyway.<br /> <br /> &quot;There's no point in trying to fix WtA's lexicon because non-English versions of the text will screw it up, but they'll screw up the existing lexicon too,&quot; just doesn't carry any weight to me. And I'm not seeing any other real debate against the idea's I'm pointing forward.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}